From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2000
From: Stuart Shelton <srcshelton@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] power: opp: accept ACPI-only configurations on !CONFIG_OF builds

In _allocate_opp_table() treat -EOPNOTSUPP from
dev_pm_opp_of_find_icc_paths() as success on non-OF builds.  The OPP
core's own icc-paths lookup is OF-only, so on ACPI-only systems it
unconditionally returns -EOPNOTSUPP and the OPP table is rejected
even though there is no icc requirement to satisfy.

Ported from srcshelton/gentoo-ebuilds:
  30196-power-opp-accept-acpi-only-configurations.patch

Signed-off-by: Stuart Shelton <srcshelton@gmail.com>
[ported: applied verbatim from srcshelton/gentoo-ebuilds
  30196-power-opp-accept-acpi-only-configurations.patch]
Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/opp/core.c b/drivers/opp/core.c
index ab0b0a2f8..3b624984a 100644
--- a/drivers/opp/core.c
+++ b/drivers/opp/core.c
@@ -1555,6 +1555,10 @@ static struct opp_table *_allocate_opp_table(struct device *dev, int index)
 
 	/* Find interconnect path(s) for the device */
 	ret = dev_pm_opp_of_find_icc_paths(dev, opp_table);
+	/* ACPI-only kernels have no OF interconnect paths to discover. */
+	if (ret == -EOPNOTSUPP && !IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_OF))
+		ret = 0;
+
 	if (ret) {
 		if (ret == -EPROBE_DEFER)
 			goto remove_opp_dev;
